    46	  `sbom_survey.cyclonedx.validate()`, which would be self-certification. From Slice 32 that
    47	  distribution must be installed: if it is missing the criterion **FAILS** naming what to install.
    48	  It does **not** skip, because an ungraded criterion is a green that means nothing (design §5.7).
    49	- **TC-97.** The only pytest configuration in this repository is `src/python/pyproject.toml`, whose
    50	  `pythonpath = ["."]` shadows an installed wheel. It is **not** an ancestor of
    51	  `scripts/sbom-survey/tests`, so pytest runs this suite with **no config file** and cannot inherit
    52	  it. Do not add a `pyproject.toml` above this directory.
    53	
    54	## Deliberately NOT wired into CI
    55	
    56	This tool is **recurring by design and NOT CI-gating** — it is **informational**
    57	(`plan-0.8.20.md` §3a, HITL 2026-07-29, steward `seq-153`).
    58	
    59	- It is **not** registered in `scripts/agent-test.sh`.
    60	- It is **not** referenced by `.github/workflows/ci.yml`.
    61	- It is **not** part of `scripts/agent-verify.sh`, `scripts/check.sh`, or any lint/typecheck scope
    62	  (`ruff` and `pyright` are scoped to `src/python`).
    63	
    64	Do not wire it in. Beyond the standing ruling, the acceptance suite is red until Slice 32 lands, so
    65	registering it would turn `main` red. `tests/test_cli.py::test_tool_declares_non_ci_gating_and_is_absent_from_ci_wiring`
    66	is the standing guard: it greps both wiring files and fails if either grows a reference.
    67	
    68	## Isolation
    69	
    70	The mini-project's own `pyproject.toml` (a Slice 32 artifact) is standalone: not a Cargo workspace
    71	member, not referenced by `src/python/pyproject.toml`, not a dependency of the root `package.json`.
    72	It can never enlarge the published dependency graph or the advisory backlog. Its own dependencies
    73	are surveyed by the tool and tagged `dev-tooling` — the tool appears in its own SBOM, by design.
    74	
    75	Generated reports go to `scripts/sbom-survey/out/`, which Slice 32 adds to `.gitignore`. Slice 33's
    76	**findings** have a separate tracked home:
    77	`dev/plans/runs/0.8.20-slice-33-library-sweep-3-FINDINGS.md` — the house convention for a dated run
    78	report, weighed against `dev/design/` and `dev/deps/` in design §5.6.
