   202	
   203	**`python/pyproject.toml` is OUT OF SCOPE, and this is the trap.** `.gitignore` line 88 ignores
   204	`/python/` **in its entirety** (root-anchored; the comment there explains it is a sourceless
   205	recovered binding kept on disk for Memex). Verified at `cbb56212`:
   206	
   207	```text
   208	$ git check-ignore -v python/pyproject.toml
   209	.gitignore:88:/python/    python/pyproject.toml   <- (TAB in real output)
   210	$ git ls-files python/
   211	(empty)
   212	```
   213	
   214	The directory does not even exist in this worktree. It is cited elsewhere in the program's records
   215	as if it were a real manifest; it is not tracked, so it is not in BOM scope, and a filesystem-walk
   216	discovery on a developer machine that *does* have it would silently pull a pinned `0.1.0` shim into
   217	the SBOM. This is the exact "noise against gitignored dev/eval lockfiles" case LBS §2 names.
   218	`git ls-files` makes it structurally impossible.
   219	
   220	**Recognized basenames — the table, and its mirror in the test oracle.** Twelve exact basenames plus
   221	one glob, in two groups:
   222	
   223	| Group | Names | Tracked matches at `cbb56212` |
   224	|---|---|---|
   225	| Matches today | `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`, `setup.py`, and the glob `requirements*.txt` | the 29 paths above |
   226	| Recognized, forward-looking | `yarn.lock`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`, `poetry.lock`, `Pipfile`, `setup.cfg` | **none** — verified: `git ls-files \| grep -E '(^\|/)(setup\.cfg\|Pipfile\|poetry\.lock\|yarn\.lock\|pnpm-lock\.yaml)$'` exits `1` with no output |
   227	
   228	The second group is present so that adding one of those files to the repo is *discovered* (and then
   229	fails REQ-4 tiering loudly) rather than silently ignored. Because none of them matches anything
   230	today, the group is a pure forward guard: it changes no discovered path and leaves §5.1's 29-path
   231	enumeration exact.
   232	
   233	⚠ **This table is mirrored 1:1 by `MANIFEST_BASENAMES` in `scripts/sbom-survey/tests/conftest.py`,
   234	and the two must be kept in lockstep.** That tuple is the oracle `AC-SBOM-03` grades against, so a
   235	name that appears here but not there is a manifest the implementation may silently skip *while the
   236	suite still reports green* — the design would state a requirement the tests do not enforce.
   237	`setup.cfg` was exactly that divergence (codex §9 round 1, fix-1 finding 1); the whole table was
   238	re-diffed against the helper when it was closed, and `poetry.lock` / `Pipfile` / `yarn.lock` /
